## 🏷️ Tag Examples

Add tags to your feature files:

```gherkin
@smoke @critical
Scenario: Critical user login
  Given User navigate to Salesforce Application
  And User Login as "Admin"
```

Then run:
```bash
# Run @smoke tests only
cross-env CUCUMBER_TAGS="@smoke" npm test

# Run @critical tests only
cross-env CUCUMBER_TAGS="@critical" npm test

# Run @smoke AND @critical
cross-env CUCUMBER_TAGS="@smoke and @critical" npm test

# Run @smoke OR @regression
cross-env CUCUMBER_TAGS="@smoke or @regression" npm test

# Run all EXCEPT @wip
cross-env CUCUMBER_TAGS="not @wip" npm test

# Complex: (@smoke or @critical) AND NOT @wip
cross-env CUCUMBER_TAGS="(@smoke or @critical) and not @wip" npm test
```

---

## 🔀 Parallel Worker Options

Adjust based on your system:

```bash
# Serial (one test at a time)
npm test
# or
cross-env CUCUMBER_WORKERS=0 npm test

# 2 parallel workers
cross-env CUCUMBER_WORKERS=2 npm test

# 4 parallel workers (default in scripts)
cross-env CUCUMBER_WORKERS=4 npm test

# 8 parallel workers (high-end systems only)
cross-env CUCUMBER_WORKERS=8 npm test
```

**System Requirements:**
- **2 workers:** Minimum (2 CPU cores)
- **4 workers:** Recommended (4 CPU cores + 8GB RAM)
- **8 workers:** High-end (8+ CPU cores + 16GB+ RAM)

